  "empirical_answers": {
    "1_standard_contract": "core.text.from-static is decl_978f0bf14d4024393c96267886ca6968 with StaticText -> Text; core.bytes.from-text is decl_a84fb8598c42e86ff66208829b86ae55 with Text -> Bytes; ByteStream is decl_e29e0ac407696662f355e9056172ac2b with exactly read op_978a7cc298584794b2e39e1c71b3e512, close op_1e147ce49f34b68b669f643f92e5213a, and read-all op_30cd44d5491201efdafea2b9e22adff0. Exact type digests and policies are recorded above.",
    "2_handler_effect": "The complete validator and normalized runtime require the starter handler to be task-effectful with explicit streams requirement closure. The accepted topology uses a task handler and a 10000-call requirement bound even though the request body is intentionally unread.",
    "3_port_zero": "Deployment contract 1 accepts 127.0.0.1:0. Both supported serve starts reported distinct actual 127.0.0.1 ports in typed ready events and served through those addresses.",
    "4_descriptor_owner": "platform/deployment.rs::DeploymentDescriptor, starter_http_deployment, validate_descriptor, and encode_deployment are the single typed owner. Contract, artifact, target, runtime, execution, HTTP/worker/stream limits, configuration, secrets, and grants are explicit descriptor fields; nested type defaults supply contract versions and unchanged conservative admission values before starter overrides.",
    "5_publication_seam": "create_project_with_hook retains GraphPublished, BeforeDescriptor, DescriptorPublished, GeneratedDirectoryPublished, and BeforeVisibility seams inside the private sibling. publish_auxiliary synchronizes the descriptor and generated directory before the existing single rename; previsibility errors remove only the owned stage.",
    "6_invalidation": "replace.body selected two compiler units. Accepted apply compiled 2, reused 4, and removed 0; subsequent check/build reused all 6. A cache-deleted clean build compiled all 6 and produced byte-identical Artifact 10 bytes.",
    "7_process_and_http_helpers": "The gate reuses the first-party bounded process/process-group owner, extracts Graph authority observation into authority.rs, and extracts the independent raw TCP HTTP/1 client into http_probe.rs. service.rs now shares those helpers without bringing PostgreSQL or lkjournal into the new gate.",
    "8_gate_ownership": "distributed_http_application is non-cacheable, depends on release_build, and is selected by product, service, and full. Release-mode preparation requires a fresh full receipt, so Docker unavailability cannot substitute for or hide the no-Docker gate.",
    "9_graceful_stop": "On the supported GNU/Linux boundary the harness owns a process group, sends SIGINT, waits with a bound, records ready/stopped and bounded logs, and reserves SIGKILL for classified cleanup. Both proof runs exited 0 with zero remaining tasks and cleanup failures.",
    "10_resources": "The release candidate, topology, compiler/artifact work, timing, CPU, RSS, response, shutdown, authority, and retained-log observations are recorded above. Exact filesystem-call, synchronized-byte, request-instruction, context-switch, provider telemetry, token, and cost dimensions are unavailable.",
    "11_checkout_and_external_state": "HEAD and origin/main equaled the audited baseline with no later commits; no nested instruction overrode the root mandate; the upstream audit found no open issue or pull request and immutable v0.1.6 remained latest. Remote state is rechecked immediately before normal push.",
